cent-color)\" stroke-width=\"2.07453\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</g>\n<defs>\n<clipPath id=\"clip0_135_313\">\n<rect width=\"42.6884\" height=\"49.3843\" fill=\"white\" transform=\"translate(0 0.793579)\"/>\n</clipPath>\n</defs>\n</svg>\n</span> Method</a></div>\n  <div class=\"wprm-layout-column-container wprm-column-gap-40 wprm-column-rows-recipe-900 meadow-main-columns\">\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-left\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-7426-ingredients\" class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients-container wprm-recipe-7426-ingredients-container wprm-block-text-normal wprm-ingredient-style-regular wprm-recipe-images-before\" data-recipe=\"7426\" data-servings=\"4\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-ingredients-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Ingredients<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-ingredients wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">4</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">pieces</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">chicken quarters</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Your choice of whole, skin-on quarters.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tbsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">olive oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For a crispy outer layer.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">To enhance flavors.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">black pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For a hint of spice.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">paprika</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Adds a smoky flavor.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">garlic powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">For extra aroma.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1/2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tsp</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">onion powder</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Complements other spices.</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">sprig</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">fresh rosemary</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Optional, for a fragrant touch.</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-7426-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7426\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Baking tray&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">Lined with foil or parchment paper for easy cleanup.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Small bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing the seasoning.</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Paper towels&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For drying the chicken.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-7426-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-7426-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"7426\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7426-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Preheat your oven to 200°C (400°F). This ensures your chicken quarters cook evenly and get that perfect crispy skin.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7426-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Pat the chicken quarters dry with paper towels. This helps the skin get nice and crispy when baking.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7426-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: In a small bowl, mix together olive oil, salt, pepper, paprika, garlic powder, and onion powder. This flavorful blend will make your chicken irresistible!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7426-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Rub the seasoning mixture evenly over each chicken quarter. Make sure to get it under the skin for extra flavor!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7426-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Place the chicken quarters skin-side up on a baking tray lined with foil or parchment paper. This makes for easy cleanup!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7426-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 6: Roast in the preheated oven for 35–45 minutes. Check that the internal temperature reaches 75°C (165°F) and the skin is golden and crispy.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-7426-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 7: Remove from the oven and let the chicken rest for 5 minutes. Garnish with fresh rosemary if desired, and serve hot. Enjoy your delicious meal!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      \n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients to whip up your delicious chicken quarter meal!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Chicken-Quarter-Recipe.webp\" alt=\"Raw chicken quarters seasoned with spices on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-7424\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Chicken-Quarter-Recipe.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ingredients-for-Chicken-Quarter-Recipe-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>4 <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken_as_food\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chicken </a>quarters</strong> – your choice of whole, skin-on quarters</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tbsp olive oil</strong> – for a crispy outer layer</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tsp salt</strong> – to enhance flavors</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 tsp black pepper</strong> – for a hint of spice</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tsp paprika</strong> – adds a smoky flavor</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 tsp garlic powder</strong> – for extra aroma</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1/2 tsp onion powder</strong> – complements other spices</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 sprig fresh rosemary</strong> – optional, for a fragrant touch</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-chicken-quarter\"><strong>How to Make Chicken Quarter</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delicious chicken quarter recipe is perfect for a quick and flavorful meal. With a preparation time of just 10 minutes and a cooking time of 35–45 minutes, you’ll have juicy, crispy chicken ready to enjoy in no time. Don’t forget to let it rest for 5 minutes before serving!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Preparation-Steps-for-Chicken-Quarter.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step preparation of chicken quarters, including preheating the oven, drying the chicken, mixing seasonings, and arranging on a baking tray.\" class=\"wp-image-7425\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Preparation-Steps-for-Chicken-Quarter.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Preparation-Steps-for-Chicken-Quarter-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your oven to 200°C (400°F). This ensures your chicken quarters cook evenly and get that perfect crispy skin.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Prepare the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pat the chicken quarters dry with paper towels. This helps the skin get nice and crispy when baking.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Make the Seasoning Mixture</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a small bowl, mix together olive oil, salt, pepper, paprika, garlic powder, and onion powder. This flavorful blend will make your chicken irresistible!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Season the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Rub the seasoning mixture evenly over each chicken quarter. Make sure to get it under the skin for extra flavor!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Arrange on Baking Tray</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Place the chicken quarters skin-side up on a baking tray lined with foil or parchment paper. This makes for easy cleanup!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Roast the Chicken</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Roast in the preheated oven for 35–45 minutes. Check that the internal temperature reaches 75°C (165°F) and the skin is golden and crispy.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Rest and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remove from the oven and let the chicken rest for 5 minutes. Garnish with fresh rosemary if desired, and serve hot. Enjoy your delicious meal!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Main Course</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>40 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>5 minutes (resting)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>55 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Not specified</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Hot and crispy</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-chicken-quarter\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Chicken Quarter</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pat the chicken dry for a crispier skin.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Marinate overnight for deeper flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a meat thermometer to ensure perfect doneness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the chicken rest before serving for juiciness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with different herbs and spices for variety.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-chicken-quarter\"><strong>How to Serve this chicken quarter</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve with a side of roasted vegetables for a colorful plate.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with creamy mashed potatoes or fluffy rice for a hearty meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with fresh herbs like parsley or cilantro for a burst of flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Accompany with a tangy lemon or garlic sauce for extra zest.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy with a crisp garden salad for a refreshing contrast.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside warm, crusty bread to soak up the juices.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For a fun twist, shred the chicken and use it in tacos or wraps.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s how to store, freeze, and reheat your chicken quarter for maximum flavor and freshness:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow chicken quarters to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in an airtight container or wrap tightly in plastic wrap.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in the refrigerator for up to 3-4 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap each chicken quarter in plastic wrap or aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place wrapped chicken in a freezer-safe bag or container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw chicken quarters in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in the oven at 350°F (175°C) for about 20-25 minutes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a meat thermometer to ensure internal temperature reaches 165°F (74°C).</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What is a chicken quarter?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>A chicken quarter refers to a cut of chicken that includes either the leg and thigh or the breast and wing. In most recipes, when we talk about chicken quarters, we are usually referring to the leg quarters, which consist of the drumstick and thigh still attached. They are known for their rich flavor and juicy texture, making them a popular choice for roasting and grilling.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What&#8217;s the best way to cook chicken leg quarters?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>The best way to cook chicken leg quarters is to bake them in the oven, which allows for even cooking and helps to retain moisture. Start by seasoning the chicken with your favorite spices and herbs, then bake at a moderate temperature until the skin is crispy and the meat is tender. You can also grill or slow-cook them for a different flavor profile, but baking is a simple and effective method that yields delicious results.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. How long to bake chicken quarters at 350 degrees?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>When baking chicken quarters at 350 degrees Fahrenheit, you should plan for about 45 to 55 minutes of cooking time. It&#8217;s important to check that the internal temperature reaches 165 degrees Fahrenheit to ensure they are fully cooked. Using a meat thermometer is a great way to confirm doneness without overcooking the chicken, which can lead to dryness.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Are chicken leg quarters healthy?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Chicken leg quarters can be a healthy option when prepared properly. They are a good source of protein and contain essential vitamins and minerals. While they do have a higher fat content compared to chicken breast, the fat is mostly unsaturated, which can be part of a balanced diet. Opting for skinless leg quarters or removing the skin after cooking can help reduce the fat content if you&#8217;re watching your intake.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We hope you’re as excited to try this juicy oven-baked chicken quarter recipe as we are! It’s simple, flavorful, and perfect for any occasion. Gather your loved ones, savor the delightful aroma, and enjoy every bite. Cooking doesn’t have to be complicated—just a little love and a great recipe can create unforgettable meals!</p>\n",
